From 3dbc7d44928059947d8cd2cb2dc43595b4e4f95b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pankaj Deopa <47059657+3-pi-radians@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:25:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Enable OpenID Connect Native SSO for mobile apps

- Implement the ThunderID DeviceSecretProvider: device secrets are JWTs
  (iss, aud, sub, jti, iat, nbf, exp, auth_id, client_id, scope, acr,
  claims, cnf.jkt) signed with the OIDC_SERVICE EC key (ES256) and then
  encrypted to a dedicated DEVICE_SECRET_ENC key (RSA-OAEP-256/A256GCM).
  Validation checks signature, issuer, expiry, required claims, the
  native SSO session (sid) and the device_sso_allowed_clients family
  list restricted to the same relying party (pairwise subjects).
  Redemptions are recorded; a sibling may sign in again while the device
  secret is valid (request replay is blocked by single-use proof and
  assertion jti).
- Add MOSIP_ESIGNET_DEVICE_SECRET_EXPIRY_SECONDS (default 24h).
- Client management: accept the RFC 8693 token-exchange grant type and
  the device_sso_allowed_clients additional_config key; map registered
  grant types to the engine client.
- Enable the token-exchange grant and advertise device_sso in
  deployment.yaml.
- Point the ThunderID replace directive at the sibling checkout that
  carries the engine changes.
- Add api-test/cmd/nativesso, a live end-to-end check of the Super App
  login, silent Child App sign-in, sign-in after the ID token expired and
  the negative cases.
